### Bug Analysis

The bug report indicates that the `CascaderSelect` component does not clear the search results after all items have been selected. This can lead to confusion for users, as they remain on the search results page without a clear way to return to the full list. The requirement is to either implement an automatic clearing mechanism or provide a button to clear the search results.

### Bug Root Cause

The root cause of the issue lies in the `handleChange` method of the `CascaderSelect` component. The current implementation does not clear the `searchValue` state when all items are selected. The relevant code already checks if the selected value length matches the data source length, but it does not take action to clear the search input in that case.

### Bug Code Snippet Location

The relevant code snippet is located in the `handleChange` method of the `components/cascader-select/cascader-select.tsx` file.

### Proposed Patch

To fix the issue, we need to ensure that the `searchValue` is cleared when all items are selected. Below is the patch that modifies the `handleChange` method accordingly.

